 "inference": [
  "Heavy machine guns (coaxial, remote station and open gunner): the own value is 760, EA's figure after 1.3.1.0, and the registry default is 890, EA's figure before it. This is the reverse of the eight cases in L3356, where the registry held EA's new number. The single-player copy of the remote HMG holds 890 in both.",
  "Light machine guns: own 600, registry 737, EA 670. Neither stored value equals EA's figure. 737 is 670 times 1.1 exactly; no stated change accounts for that factor, and it is noted only as arithmetic.",
  "The rule 'where a registry row exists, use its default' (L3356) therefore has a known exception in this property. Until an in-game timing settles it, the site should not state a vehicle machine gun velocity as certain; for the HMG, 760 has EA's statement behind it.",
  "A later EA note that changed these velocities again would also explain the rows, but the two notes on file (1.3.1.0 and 1.3.3.0) hold no such line."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Which velocity applies in a match. Test from L3335: fire the coaxial HMG at a wall 380 m away and time the flight (0.5 s means 760, 0.43 s means 890). For the LMG at 300 m: 0.5 s means 600, 0.45 s means 670, 0.41 s means 737.",
  "EA notes after 1.3.3.0 are not on file."
 ],
